WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.459 --> 00:00:07.009
Speaker 1: You know, we spoke last week about
how many companies that were celebrating Pride

00:00:07.009 --> 00:00:12.170
Month have a long history of donating to homophobic
politicians.

00:00:12.170 --> 00:00:17.859
I want to now follow up on a story that we
talked about some time ago, several months

00:00:17.859 --> 00:00:18.859
ago.

00:00:18.859 --> 00:00:27.189
The company Boeing has quietly resumed donating
to the Republican traders that some know as

00:00:27.189 --> 00:00:30.439
the Sedition Caucus.

00:00:30.439 --> 00:00:33.800
This is a Daily Beast article which outlines
what's going on really well.

00:00:33.800 --> 00:00:35.059
Let's take a look at it.

00:00:35.059 --> 00:00:39.710
And it says, After briefly swearing off political
donations in the wake of the Capitol riot,

00:00:39.710 --> 00:00:45.620
Boeing is now throwing cash at officials who
fought to overturn the results of the 2020

00:00:45.620 --> 00:00:46.620
election.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.170
In a recent filing with the Federal Election
Commission, Boeing's political action committee

00:00:51.170 --> 00:00:56.230
reported major contributions to three Republican
members of Congress who voted to challenge

00:00:56.230 --> 00:00:57.899
the results of the Electoral College.

00:00:57.899 --> 00:01:05.309
Steve Scalise, disgusting guy, and then the
lesser known Vicky Hartzler and Jack Burgmann.

00:01:05.309 --> 00:01:10.740
The report being boings first to show political
contributions after the assault on the Capitol,

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.320
also disclosed a twenty five thousand dollar
gift to the Republican Attorneys General Association,

00:01:16.320 --> 00:01:21.810
whose fundraising armed arm helped promote
the January six rally to, quote, stop the

00:01:21.810 --> 00:01:23.110
steel.

00:01:23.110 --> 00:01:28.320
Boeing contributed less than half that amount
to the organization's Democratic counterpart.

00:01:28.320 --> 00:01:32.659
Boeing gave Scarless and Hartzler each five
thousand dollars the limit for an election.

00:01:32.659 --> 00:01:38.170
Burgman, a Michigan conservative who in December
pushed erroneous claims of election fraud

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:43.430
in his home state, got half of that amount
Boeing previously donated to all three.

00:01:43.430 --> 00:01:47.570
Now, the article does go on to say Boeing
also gave money to Democratic officials like

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:52.570
Nancy Pelosi, as well as Republicans who did
vote to certify the election results.

00:01:52.570 --> 00:01:57.520
The aerospace and defense giant also gave
the maximum one hundred and five thousand

00:01:57.520 --> 00:02:02.250
dollars to both parties, House and Senate
campaign committees.

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.020
This is what people really have to understand
about this.

00:02:05.020 --> 00:02:11.130
First of all, the headline is Boeing quietly
resumes donating to Republican, you know,

00:02:11.130 --> 00:02:12.520
to the Sedition Caucus.

00:02:12.520 --> 00:02:14.660
I call them the Republican traitors.

00:02:14.660 --> 00:02:20.440
It may be worse than that because Boeing may
never really have stopped the donations to

00:02:20.440 --> 00:02:21.440
these people.

00:02:21.440 --> 00:02:26.850
And what I mean by that is when the January
6th riots happened in early twenty twenty

00:02:26.850 --> 00:02:29.380
one, obviously twenty twenty was over.

00:02:29.380 --> 00:02:31.880
So twenty twenty contributions were done.

00:02:31.880 --> 00:02:36.410
The twenty twenty election was over and the
twenty, twenty calendar year was also over.

00:02:36.410 --> 00:02:42.830
Now it's twenty twenty one and they are again
making contributions, so even to say that

00:02:42.830 --> 00:02:49.610
they stopped them between January and June
when donations are really only now ramping

00:02:49.610 --> 00:02:54.950
up and they've hit their maximums anyway,
is it really even fair to say they stopped

00:02:54.950 --> 00:03:00.180
anything because they're donating in June
instead of in February or March or April or

00:03:00.180 --> 00:03:01.180
May?

00:03:01.180 --> 00:03:04.970
It's not even clear to me that there was anything
to the statement that they were stopping those

00:03:04.970 --> 00:03:09.970
donations to these traitorous, seditious individuals.

00:03:09.970 --> 00:03:15.630
We had this example earlier in the week specifically
about Boeing and about boycotts.

00:03:15.630 --> 00:03:22.640
It's really hard to boycott a company like
Boeing because for the most part, Boeing is,

00:03:22.640 --> 00:03:27.480
number one, a defense contractor, and it has
nothing to do with sort of consumer facing

00:03:27.480 --> 00:03:29.690
decisions that we make up.

00:03:29.690 --> 00:03:37.100
If we wanted to boycott Boeing as our airline
passengers, we would have to figure out, OK,

00:03:37.100 --> 00:03:38.100
let's see.

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:40.080
I need to go from New York City to Paris.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:46.730
Which airlines are flying Airbus planes or
is there some other way that I can get to

00:03:46.730 --> 00:03:49.910
Florida without flying on a Boeing airplane?

00:03:49.910 --> 00:03:52.360
It's really difficult to do this.

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.460
How do you even boycott Boeing?

00:03:54.460 --> 00:03:57.300
And that's part of what makes this so pernicious.

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:02.450
Now, this is not the only company that is
making donations, again, to the traitorous,

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:08.610
treasonous Republicans, Pfizer, Intel, Ford,
Cigna, AT&amp;T.

00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:14.310
They've continued to donate to political action
committees that support many of these Republican

00:04:14.310 --> 00:04:17.209
members of the House and Senate.

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:22.320
So to me, this is once again a calculated
public relations move.

00:04:22.320 --> 00:04:28.099
They wanted those initial headlines to say
they are stopping the donations to people

00:04:28.099 --> 00:04:33.240
in the House and Senate who supported Stop
the Steel and may have, you know, deliberately

00:04:33.240 --> 00:04:41.110
or implicitly supported this January six writes,
It's not even clear it ever really even meant

00:04:41.110 --> 00:04:44.650
anything because there are limits on political
donations.

00:04:44.650 --> 00:04:49.479
And they waited a few months to say that they
were paused maybe of no meaning whatsoever.

00:04:49.479 --> 00:04:51.930
And we've talked about other other examples
of this.

00:04:51.930 --> 00:04:56.430
Last week, I had the story for you about how
many companies that are now saying we celebrate

00:04:56.430 --> 00:05:03.780
Pride Month have donated to both candidates
and political action committees that support

00:05:03.780 --> 00:05:08.150
candidates that are homophobic and that have
lobbied against gay marriage.

00:05:08.150 --> 00:05:12.599
And in the, you know, the days where that
was the fight and now against so-called religious

00:05:12.599 --> 00:05:17.999
freedom to discriminate against people who
are or are perceived to be part of the LGBT

00:05:17.999 --> 00:05:18.999
community.

00:05:18.999 --> 00:05:22.610
We've talked about companies who, in the wake
of the George Floyd protests around police

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:29.650
brutality, loudly announced we're sending
managers to implicit bias training, which

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:34.479
is not even clear, really has any connection
whatsoever to many of the problems that we're

00:05:34.479 --> 00:05:37.009
dealing with as far as race goes in the United
States.

00:05:37.009 --> 00:05:40.180
And it was an obvious and brazen PR move.

00:05:40.180 --> 00:05:41.980
This is much the same thing.

00:05:41.980 --> 00:05:45.210
And so am I saying boycott Boeing or don't
boycott Boeing?

00:05:45.210 --> 00:05:46.600
No, I'm not saying anything about that.

00:05:46.600 --> 00:05:47.770
This is not about cancelation.

00:05:47.770 --> 00:05:52.439
This is about understand even something like
Amazon when they announced a couple of years

00:05:52.439 --> 00:05:55.110
ago, we now pay everybody fifteen bucks an
hour.

00:05:55.110 --> 00:05:56.110
Wow.

00:05:56.110 --> 00:05:57.110
OK, that's great.

00:05:57.110 --> 00:06:00.810
Well, OK, but what was the PR benefit of that
relative to the cost.

00:06:00.810 --> 00:06:05.330
And of course it doesn't apply to third party
contractors that Amazon contracts with and

00:06:05.330 --> 00:06:08.180
there's so many loopholes and end runs around
it.

00:06:08.180 --> 00:06:15.520
These are mostly public relations decisions
and there is now a sort of industry based

00:06:15.520 --> 00:06:20.150
around making these types of announcements
while behind the scenes they keep donating

00:06:20.150 --> 00:06:26.000
to the homophobic politicians, they keep donating
to the the sedition bunch or whatever you

00:06:26.000 --> 00:06:27.590
want to call them.

00:06:27.590 --> 00:06:32.710
And if there is really going to be change
that we want to see, we're going to have to

00:06:32.710 --> 00:06:34.889
demand more of these companies.

00:06:34.889 --> 00:06:36.960
This is really not going to cut it.

00:06:36.960 --> 00:06:43.749
And we should all be not endlessly cynical,
but healthily skeptical when we see such pronouncements

00:06:43.749 --> 00:06:45.770
made by these corporations.

00:06:45.770 --> 00:06:49.229
We'll have more examples of this on The David
Pakman Show Instagram.

00:06:49.229 --> 00:08:11.419
You can follow us there at David 

